#: src/setting-variables-from-the-command-line.md:1
msgid "Setting Variables from the Command Line"
msgstr ""

#: src/setting-variables-from-the-command-line.md:3
msgid "Variables can be overridden from the command line."
msgstr ""

#: src/setting-variables-from-the-command-line.md:5
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"os := \"linux\"\n"
"\n"
"test: build\n"
"  ./test --test {{os}}\n"
"\n"
"build:\n"
"  ./build {{os}}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/setting-variables-from-the-command-line.md:21
msgid ""
"Any number of arguments of the form `NAME=VALUE` can be passed before "
"recipes:"
msgstr ""

#: src/setting-variables-from-the-command-line.md:29
msgid "Or you can use the `--set` flag:"
msgstr ""

#: src/setting-variables-from-the-command-line.md:37
msgid ""
"Variables in submodules can be overridden using the `::`\\-separated path to "
"the variable. A variable named `bar` in a submodule named `foo` may be "
"overridden with `foo::bar=VALUE` or `--set foo::bar VALUE`."
msgstr ""
